cff-version: 1.2.0
title: UK marine fishing closures
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it. The closure boundaries and
  restriction summaries are public sector information under the Open
  Government Licence v3.0; the assembled list and the restriction
  classification are CAUGHT's own.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: CAUGHT
    website: https://caught.org.uk
    email: contact@caught.org.uk
abstract: >-
  Every legally closed fishing area in UK and Crown Dependency waters that
  CAUGHT monitors: 271 closures with their boundary, what the rule prohibits,
  the instrument that creates it and the authority that made it. There is no
  single official list — the rules are made by fifteen authorities under their
  own instruments and sea fisheries are devolved — so this is that
  reconciliation. Boundaries are simplified for display and must not be used to
  decide whether a position falls inside a closure. No vessel is named.
keywords:
  - marine protected areas
  - fishing closures
  - bottom trawling
  - scallop dredging
  - no-take zones
  - marine conservation
  - United Kingdom
  - fisheries management
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/angus-e-mcmillan/caught-uk-closures
url: https://caught.org.uk/data
